      "locked": false,
      "text": "RESEARCH NOTES / sources used for the claims in this board",
      "originalText": "RESEARCH NOTES / sources used for the claims in this board",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "fontWeight": "700"
    },
    {
      "id": "text-152",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 2985,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 140.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#243247",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1203688,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 15918808,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. FAISS indexes + guidelines (official): github.com/facebookresearch/faiss/wiki/Faiss-indexes\n   IndexFlatIP is exact; normalized vectors support cosine-style search; HNSW / IVF trade recall, memory, and speed.\n2. Two-stage retrieval evidence: arxiv.org/abs/2212.06121 and arxiv.org/abs/2205.10569\n   Dense retrieval supplies candidates; cross-encoder/reranker improves precision at added latency.\n3. Jev public interface: jevtypesafeai.com/jev/architecture and getmaxim.ai/articles/what-is-jev-system-one-model/\n   Choice is documented as up to 255 options; this is a product/interface limit, not a universal single-pass limit.\n4. Nebius Token Factory docs: docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/api-reference/examples/create-embeddings\n   OpenAI-compatible embeddings/chat are the implementation basis in this repository.",
      "originalText": "1. FAISS indexes + guidelines (official): github.com/facebookresearch/faiss/wiki/Faiss-indexes\n   IndexFlatIP is exact; normalized vectors support cosine-style search; HNSW / IVF trade recall, memory, and speed.\n2. Two-stage retrieval evidence: arxiv.org/abs/2212.06121 and arxiv.org/abs/2205.10569\n   Dense retrieval supplies candidates; cross-encoder/reranker improves precision at added latency.\n3. Jev public interface: jevtypesafeai.com/jev/architecture and getmaxim.ai/articles/what-is-jev-system-one-model/\n   Choice is documented as up to 255 options; this is a product/interface limit, not a universal single-pass limit.\n4. Nebius Token Factory docs: docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/api-reference/examples/create-embeddings\n   OpenAI-compatible embeddings/chat are the implementation basis in this repository.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "fontWeight": "400"
    },
    {
      "id": "text-153",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 3185,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 21.6,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#dc2626",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1211607,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 16023537,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Evidence discipline: CentRI is a design for predictable scaling, not a guaranteed accuracy win. The decisive next artifact is a reproducible benchmark harness.",
      "originalText": "Evidence discipline: CentRI is a design for predictable scaling, not a guaranteed accuracy win. The decisive next artifact is a reproducible benchmark harness.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "fontWeight": "700"
    }
